or मूर्छ् cl. 1. P. (Dhātup. vii, 32) मूर्छति (pf. मुमूर्छ, MBh.; Kāv. &c.; aor. अमूर्छीत् Gr.; fut. मूर्छिता, मूर्छिष्यति, ib.; ind.p., मूर्त्वा, ib.),
to become solid, thicken, congeal, assume shape or substance or consistency, expand, increase, grow, become or be vehement or intense or strong, AV. &c. &c.;
to fill, pervade, penetrate, spread over, Kālid.;
 to have power or take effect upon (loc.), ib.;
to grow stiff or rigid, faint, swoon, become senseless or stupid or unconscious, MBh.; Kāv. &c.;
to deafen, Caurap.;
to cause to sound aloud, MBh. :
Caus. मूर्छयति (mc. also ˚ते), to cause to thicken or coagulate (milk), Kauś.;
to cause to settle into a fixed or solid form, shape, AitUp.;
to strengthen, rouse, excite, MBh.; R.;
to cause to sound loudly, play (a musical instrument), BhP.

